EXT. HIGH DESERT WINDMILL - DAY

A creaking windmill over a stock tank. Three riders sit their horses in the shade.

                    EZRA
          Water's low.

                    HATTIE
          Water's always low.

                    EZRA
          Then why're we out here?

                    HATTIE
          Because Tom says the old man buried something under this mill.

                    TOM
          I never said that.

                    HATTIE
          You said it Tuesday.

                    TOM
          I said somebody told me a man told me.

                    EZRA
          That's three hands removed from nothing.

                    HATTIE
          Dig.

                    TOM
          With what?

                    HATTIE
          Your spurs.

                    EZRA
          Hattie, I'm too old to dig.

                    HATTIE
          Then watch Tom.

                    TOM
          I'm not digging, either.

                    EZRA
          Well, somebody better.

A long wind moves through the blades. The mill creaks. The three sit and look at one another.
